## 4. Free and Premium Access Rules

Implement the following access policy.

### A. Two globally designated free tests

Maintain the existing business rule that the administrator can designate:

- One free Sectional Test across the entire platform.
- One free PYQ Test across the entire platform.

These are two individual free tests in total, not two free tests per subject.

No Full-Length Test should be free by default.

The administrator must be able to configure which individual Sectional Test and which individual PYQ Test are free.

If the platform has no designated free test for a category, do not automatically make another test free.

The two designated free tests must be accessible without purchasing their respective subject series, subject to the normal authentication and attempt rules.

### B. Premium tests

All other tests are premium by default.

A student who has not purchased a particular subject's test series must not be allowed to attempt its premium tests.

However, the student must still be allowed to:

- Browse the subject.
- Browse all three test categories.
- See individual test names and numbers.
- See test duration and question count when that information is intended to be public.
- See whether a test is free, locked, purchased, or completed.
- View the subject's test-series price.
- Open the payment page to purchase the complete subject series.

Do not hide the test catalogue merely because a student has not purchased access.

### C. Purchase scope

The purchase unit is the complete subject test series, not an individual test.

For example, if Political Science has 15 Sectional Tests, 10 Full-Length Tests, and 5 PYQ Tests, a successful Political Science purchase should grant access to all eligible premium tests included in that subject's series.

Do not create a separate payment requirement for each test.

If a subject has a different number of tests, calculate access dynamically based on the tests assigned to that subject.

The two globally designated free tests remain free regardless of whether the student has purchased the associated subject series.

