## 6. Locked-Test Click Behavior

This is one of the most important requirements.

When a student clicks a premium test without having purchased the relevant subject series, do not display a raw HTTP 403 error or an inaccessible test-instructions page.

Instead, redirect the student to the relevant subject-series purchase page.

### Required flow

1. Student opens a subject.
2. Student selects a test category.
3. Student sees the available tests.
4. Student clicks a locked premium test.
5. Frontend checks the student's subject-series access status.
6. If access is missing, navigate to the purchase page for that test's subject.
7. Show the selected test name and clearly explain that purchasing the complete subject series unlocks it.
8. Display the subject-series price and included categories.
9. Offer a prominent **Purchase Subject Test Series** button.
10. After successful verified payment, return the student to the original test or the subject's test catalogue.

Example route:

`/subjects/:subjectId/purchase`

Use the existing routing conventions if they differ.

Preserve the intended destination using a validated internal route or equivalent state so the student can return to the selected test after payment.

Do not trust an arbitrary redirect URL supplied by the browser. Prevent open-redirect vulnerabilities.

### Required purchase-page message

Display a clear message similar to:

"You haven't purchased the Political Science Test Series yet. Purchase the complete subject series to unlock all eligible premium Sectional Tests, Full-Length Tests, and PYQ Tests included in this package."

Also explain that the designated free tests remain available without purchasing the subject series.

Use the actual subject name dynamically. Do not hardcode Political Science into every page.

### Authentication behavior

If the student is not logged in:

1. Preserve the selected test or purchase destination.
2. Redirect the student to the existing login or registration flow.
3. After successful authentication, return the student to the relevant subject purchase page.
4. Never create an order for an unauthenticated user.

Do not bypass or replace the existing authentication system.

