## 13. Protect Premium Test Content

A premium test must remain protected even if someone bypasses the frontend.

For example, a user must not gain access by manually entering a test URL, changing a React state variable, modifying browser storage, or calling the API directly.

Enforce access checks on the backend before returning protected test instructions or question content, starting an attempt, saving answers, submitting an attempt, or retrieving protected results.

Use the existing authentication system and verify the authenticated user on every protected request.

The backend must derive the user identity from the authenticated session or token, not from an arbitrary `userId` supplied in the request body.

A free test may bypass the subject-purchase requirement, but it must still obey normal authentication, test-publication, attempt-limit, and result-access rules.

Do not expose correct answers or solutions through public catalogue endpoints.

Do not weaken the test-taking or one-attempt rules while implementing payments.

