## 18. Testing Requirements

Add automated tests or reliable repeatable test procedures for the following cases.

### Free tests

1. An authenticated student can access the globally designated free Sectional Test without purchasing its subject series.
2. An authenticated student can access the globally designated free PYQ Test without purchasing its subject series.
3. Other tests do not become free accidentally.
4. A Full-Length Test remains premium unless the business rules are explicitly changed.

### Premium tests

5. A student without a subject-series purchase can browse premium test names and public metadata.
6. The same student cannot retrieve premium question content directly from the backend.
7. Clicking a locked test redirects the student to the correct subject's purchase page.
8. A student cannot use a purchase in one subject to unlock another subject.
9. A successful purchase unlocks all eligible premium tests in the purchased subject.
10. The student does not have to purchase every test individually.
11. The student cannot purchase the same active package again unnecessarily.
12. Existing attempt and retake restrictions continue to work.

### Payment security

13. A failed payment does not grant access.
14. A pending payment does not grant access prematurely.
15. A forged or invalid signature does not grant access.
16. An amount mismatch does not grant access.
17. A payment belonging to a different order or user does not grant access.
18. Duplicate webhook events do not create duplicate purchases.
19. Repeated verification requests do not corrupt the order or entitlement.
20. A frontend success message alone cannot unlock a package.
21. Unauthenticated users cannot create valid purchases or obtain entitlements.
22. Non-admin users cannot change package prices or free-test configuration.

### User experience

23. The current raw HTTP 403 experience is replaced by the intended purchase flow when the specific problem is missing subject-series access.
24. The student returns to the intended test or catalogue after successful payment.
25. The UI handles cancelled checkout, failed payment, pending verification, and network errors.
26. Mobile and desktop layouts remain usable.
27. The purchase page shows the correct dynamic subject, price, and included tests.

